{"lc": 1, "type": "constructor", "id": ["langchain", "schema", "document", "Document"], "kwargs": {"metadata": {"thread_id": "2866601_2866599", "turn_ids": ["2866601_2866599", "2866600_2866602", "2866603_2866604", "2866605_2866606"], "root_turns": ["2866601_2866599"]}, "page_content": "Customer: text: @SpotifyCares is there a way to know if I\u2019m adding a duplicate song within a folder of music?\nAgent: text: @796169 Hey Jael! You should be prompted if the song's already in your playlist and give you the option to \"Skip Duplicate\" or \"Add Anyway\". Hope this helps. If you have any other questions, just give us a shout \ud83d\ude42 /KC\n  Customer: text: @SpotifyCares But what about playlists within a folder. It\u2019s different. Maybe not though\n  Agent: text: @796169 The same prompt should show up if you add duplicate tracks to a playlist within a folder. Could you tell us the make/model of your device, as well as the operating system and Spotify version you're using? /KB\n    Customer: text: @SpotifyCares iPhone/MacBook latest versions. So if I have the same song in playlist 1, and playlist 7 in a folder it should prompt me?\n    Agent: text: @796169 The \"Skip Duplicate\" prompt up is specific to playlists only, not folder content. We can see how that\u2019d be handy, though. We'll let the right team know it's something you'd like to see /KB\n      Customer: text: @SpotifyCares Thank you, appreciate it!\n      Agent: text: @796169 No worries. Feel free to tweet us if there's anything else. https://t.co/uEkAlnxbzn /GK", "type": "Document"}}